<title>CANADA: Donohue to sell Manitoulin land holdings.</title>
<headline>Donohue to sell Manitoulin land holdings.</headline>
<dateline>MONTREAL 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Donohue Inc said on Friday that it was seeking to sell its Manitoulin Land Holdings in Northern Ontario for C$21.5 million.</p>
<p>The land comprises 75,000 acres and 55 miles of Lake Huron shoreline, and represents one of the largest private land holdings in Ontario, Donohue said. The property includes 45,000 acres on Manitoulin Island, the world's largest freshwater island and 30,000 acres on neighboring Cockburn Island.</p>
<p>The property has potential for recreational use and has extensive timber resources, limestone reserves and aggregate deposits. The property is listed with Collier Macaulay Nicolls.</p>
<p>((Reuters Montreal bureau 514-985-2434))</p>
